{
  "_readme": [
    "This file is what makes the inspector say 'this deviates from the design system'.",
    "",
    "  name      — what the component is called (same name as in Figma).",
    "  match     — CSS selectors your prototypes use for it. Lets the tool recognise",
    "              a component WITHOUT editing prototype HTML.",
    "  figma     — Figma URL for the component. A file-level link works; paste the",
    "              component's node URL (right-click the component > Copy link) to",
    "              deep-link straight to it.",
    "  figmaPath — where it sits in the library, shown as a breadcrumb in the panel.",
    "  story     — Storybook/Chromatic URL for the coded component. Present = 'exists",
    "              in code, use the real one'; absent with a figma link = 'design only'.",
    "  library   — which published library owns it.",
    "  code      — where the real component lives, for the developer.",
    "  variants  — what each variant is SUPPOSED to look like. This is the spec.",
    "              Values are token names (--teal-primary) or literals (5px).",
    "              Use '*' as the variant name if the rule applies to all variants.",
    "",
    "No 'variants' block means the tool can only check whether values are tokens.",
    "A 'variants' block means it can tell you exactly what is wrong.",
    "The 'match' selectors also tell the tool which CSS is the component's own —",
    "any matched rule that reaches beyond them (contextual ancestors, ids, foreign",
    "classes) is reported as a change on top of the design system."
  ],
